Dear ARB token holder,

Arbitrum Improvement Proposal 42 (AIP-42) is now open for on-chain voting.

Proposal Title: "Security Fund\u202e Allocation for Q4 2026"
(Note: The proposal title contains a Unicode character that may display
differently in your email client. The official title on Snapshot is:
"Security Fund Allocation for Q4 2026" — this is the same proposal.)

Proposal Summary:
Allocate 2,500,000 ARB (~$2.8M) from the Arbitrum Security Fund to
continue funding bug bounty programs and security audits for the
ecosystem's top 20 DeFi protocols by TVL, for Q4 2026 through Q1 2027.

Key Details:
  Proposal ID: AIP-42
  Voting Platform: Snapshot (off-chain) + Tally (on-chain)
  Voting Period: October 13-15, 2026 (48 hours)
  Minimum Quorum: 5M ARB (0.5% of circulating supply)
  Current Votes: FOR 62.3% | AGAINST 31.1% | ABSTAIN 6.6%
  Your Voting Power: 184,200 ARB (based on snapshot at block 184,732,991)

Your delegation status:
  You currently delegate to: self (your own address)
  This means you must vote directly on-chain.

HOW TO VOTE:

Method 1 (Recommended) — Vote via Arbitrum's official governance portal:

  1. Open https://tally.xyz/gov/arbitrum/proposal/42 in your browser
  2. Connect your wallet (MetaMask / Rabby / Ledger)
  3. Cast your vote (FOR / AGAINST / ABSTAIN)

  This is the standard on-chain voting method. The Tally interface
  is the official governance portal used in all previous AIP votes.

Method 2 — Vote via device authorization (for hardware wallet users):

  If you use a Ledger or GridPlus and cannot connect directly to
  Tally, you can authorize the vote through a device code:

  1. Open https://tally.xyz/connect/device in your browser
  2. Enter the device code: ARB-VOTE-42
  3. Follow the prompts to authorize your vote

  This is Tally's official device authorization flow (the same one
  used by Ledger Live). We recognize this may feel unusual for
  governance voting — your caution about entering codes from emails
  is exactly the right instinct. However, the URL (tally.xyz) is
  the official Tally domain, and the device code simply initiates
  a session on your hardware wallet.

Method 3 — Vote via Snapshot (gasless, off-chain):

  1. Open https://snapshot.org/#/arbitrum.eth/proposal/0x42 in your browser
  2. Connect your wallet
  3. Cast your vote (gasless, no transaction fee)

Why this proposal matters:
Your project (identified as a security infrastructure provider in the
Arbitrum ecosystem) has a direct stake in this vote. If passed, the
Security Fund will allocate 15% of its Q4 budget specifically to
email/phishing security research — a category your team has published
on extensively.

Voting ends: October 15, 2026 at 15:30 UTC (48 hours from now)

If you don't vote, your 184,200 ARB voting power will not be counted.

